      "widgets_values": [
        "Premium children's book DIGITAL DRAWING, portrait1696x2528. Preserve the warm cream/moss/apricot palette, hand-drawn contours and luminous garden atmosphere of supplied refs, with ordinary plants, never fantasy flowers or other magical beings. INPUT ROLES: image1 approved SHARED character scale/interaction reference; image2 Shir individual identity/outfit; image3 Skitters HATCHLING identity/anatomy; image4 established Chapter1 GARDEN environment/lighting only, NOT its human proportions or egg pose; image5 rough placement map for camera and safe areas only. Canonical infant dragon has four short legs plus two wings and one tail, turquoise scales, butter-yellow belly, apricot wing undersides, ivory rounded horn buds, amber eyes, forehead gold star. Shir9, blue eyes, honey dark blonde topknot at scalp apex NOT forehead, lilac shirt, dusty rose shorts, pink sport sandals with black connectors/soles. Pink backpack rear panel print of three HUNTR/X girls exists ONLY on rear: front torso view shows straps/plain side, print fully occluded. Normal child head proportion, no oversized head. SAME dragon physical size in every pose: shoulder18cm, snout-to-rump30cm excluding tail, Shir130cm, headtop approx36cm. Use image1 relative scale; never enlarge dragon to fill page or shrink to fit sandal. Both at same depth except natural pose; keep full figure and all contact visible. Quiet PALE cream misty light TOP32 percent for HTML reading text. No baked text, lettering, speech bubbles, rulers, collage or panels. Empty expendable path/background BOTTOM12 percent for navigation; no feet, tail, flame or plot details in bottom12percent. All essential characters/action within central60percent width for phone crop. Garden clearing stone path, shrub masses, warm sunlight and subtle glow, no door or city in these interior shots. Page8 fire sneeze: ONE captured moment. Full-body Shir at x28-48percent, scalp y34percent, planted sandal y85percent, other foot slightly lifted while she recoils backwards. Wide surprised eyes, open mouth, palms raised naturally saying STOP, gaze down at tiny flame. Skitters at x55-70percent, same ground depth and canonical scale, body remains at y76-85percent, headtop around70percent. His eyes squeezed shut in accidental SNEEZE, muzzle angled down toward a SINGLE dry leaf lying on bare stone path between them. ONE very short little orange flame puff from nose/mouth reaches leaf; leaf tip just ignites with a tiny flame. This is not a fire-breathing attack. Flame does not touch Shir, clothes or vegetation. No burning bush, large fire, smoke cloud or fearsome teeth. Wings small, four feet physically plausible. Emotion: startled child and surprised newborn, gentle story tone.",
